A vector space over a field F is a set V, denoted as V(F). The elements of F are called scalars, whereas the elements of V are called vectors. Together with two operations of vector addition and scalar multiplication, the following axioms hold:
Vector Spaces
Vector Spaces
1. ∀ x, y ∈ V, there is a unique sum x + y ∈ V (closed under addition)
x + y = y + x} commutative law
