Linear Dependence
Linear dependence of a set of vectors
A set of vectors x1, x2 · · · , xn in linear space (X , F ), is said to be linearly dependent iff there exist scalars α1, α2, · · · , αn ∈ F , not all zero, such that
α1x1 + α2x2 + · · · + αnxn = 0.
If the only set of αi for which above holds is α1 = 0, α2 = 0, · · · , αn = 0, then the set of vectors x1, x2, · · · , xn is said to be linearly independent.
• For a dependent set of vectors, infinitely many choices of coefficients.
• Finding one such choice of coefficients suffices.
